1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,759
The Law of Conservation of Energy says energy can't be created or destroyed,

2
00:00:04,759 --> 00:00:09,271
only transferred from one store to another, so the total stays the same.

3
00:00:09,271 --> 00:00:12,918
A pendulum swaps potential and kinetic energy as it swings.

4
00:00:13,980 --> 00:00:17,565
Energy diagrams show this. For every 100 joules supplied,

5
00:00:17,565 --> 00:00:22,386
an old incandescent lamp gives only 10 joules of light and 90 joules of heat.

6
00:00:22,386 --> 00:00:25,909
An LED lamp gives 75 joules of light and only 25 of heat.

7
00:00:26,971 --> 00:00:32,533
The 'lost' energy hasn't vanished; it has gone to stores that aren't useful, mostly heat.

8
00:00:32,533 --> 00:00:36,984
Efficiency measures how much of the input energy becomes useful output.

9
00:00:36,984 --> 00:00:41,063
Efficient devices waste less, which helps protect the environment.
